VIRELAI_WORLD_MODEL_MANUAL = (
    "\n\nHow Virelai helps:\n"
    "Virelai is your persistent observational memory, not another player. It watches the same run, connects objects across frames, compiles witnessed action-effect rules, records exact win boundaries, and compares consecutive levels. Its claims distinguish OBSERVED evidence from CANDIDATE, INFERRED, CONTRADICTED, and UNKNOWN content. It never chooses or consumes an environment action.\n"
    "Use `virelai('world')` when you need the accumulated world model rather than re-deriving it from the current frame. Use `virelai('diff')` after a level change to see which structural types recur and which are new. Use `virelai('object', id=...)` or `virelai('mechanic', id=...)` for one focused record. Use `virelai('model_evidence', id=...)` when a claim matters enough to inspect its witnesses. Raw transition queries remain available through `virelai('help')`.\n"
    "Do not call Virelai mechanically every turn. Call it when past evidence can answer a concrete question, when memory would otherwise be reconstructed, when an action effect is uncertain, or when a new level must be compared with earlier experience. Ask for the smallest useful view.\n"
    "After any observed win, whether produced by you or another actor, treat the saved WinRecord as valuable evidence. At the new level, consult the world model and level diff before discarding prior knowledge. Recover: the winning action and boundary; earlier failures of that same action; established prior mechanics; recurring structural types; and new or unexplained types. Use these facts to form a concrete new-level goal, while keeping the cause of the prior win UNKNOWN unless the evidence actually establishes it.\n"
    "Virelai reports remembered observations and bounded interpretations. You remain responsible for judging relevance, reconfirming transferred behavior, planning, and acting.\n"
)


